WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:12.367
Bottom line: Copilot is a family, not one tool; choose Chat, Microsoft 365, GitHub, or Studio by job, then verify access, licensing, and grounding.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.867
Copilot Chat fits research and drafting.

00:00:15.867 --> 00:00:25.267
It can summarize web information, rewrite content, analyze files, create images, use agents, and ask supported work questions.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.600
Microsoft 365 Copilot brings AI into work apps.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:38.367
Grounding, user permissions, compliance controls and license level shape what it can answer for each person.

00:00:38.933 --> 00:00:43.133
GitHub Copilot fits coding workflows in developer tools.

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:51.300
Copilot Studio builds agents and workflows connected to organizational data, systems, and channels for teams.

00:00:51.867 --> 00:00:54.533
Make the decision after the fit is clear.

00:00:54.533 --> 00:01:01.800
Check permissions, license tier, and grounding so leaders know what each output can and cannot use in practice.
